course: dictionary
lesson: 11757
title: Banner: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A banner is a long piece of cloth or paper with words or pictures on it. People hang it up or carry it so others can read it from far away. «The class hung a welcome banner above the door.»
explain: Banner can also mean a wide advert or heading across a web page. «Click the banner at the top of the page to see the free game.» The word stays the same, but its meaning depends on where it is used. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Look for clues. In «The marchers carried banners through the town», the word marchers shows it is a cloth sign, not a web advert. «The team played under the banner of the local club» uses a phrase: under the banner of means under the name or idea of a group.
fact: A banner is a long piece of cloth or paper with words or pictures on it.
fact: «Banner» can mean a wide advert or heading across a web page.
fact: «Banner» can also mean a flag, but this is an old use.
fact: «Under the banner of» means under the name or idea of a group.
fact: People carry banners at protests, and schools hang them up for events like sports day.
exercise: «The school hung a big banner saying Welcome Back.» What is a banner here? | A type of boat | A quiet whisper | *A long piece of cloth or paper with words on it | A small coin
exercise: «The shop put a banner across the top of the web page.» What does banner mean here? | A kind of bird | A long walk in the country | *A wide advert or heading across a web page | A cloth bag for shopping
exercise: «The singers performed under the banner of the choir.» What does under the banner of mean? | *Under the name or idea of a group | Far away from the choir | Hiding from a crowd | Underneath a table
test: «The old ship sailed with its banner flying in the wind.» What does banner mean here? | A web advert | A heading on a page | *A flag (an old use) | A type of sail rope
test: Why do protesters carry banners? | *To show what their group believes | To make a bridge over a river | To sell cakes to the crowd | To keep the sun off their heads
exam: Which sentence uses banner to mean a web advert? | The team won under the banner of the school | The banner was made of blue cloth | *Click the banner at the top of the page for a free game | The children made a banner for sports day
